  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "iLQ9zr2NkxEAgL/9m1taPfnLzYU=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:11.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The executor worker pool moves job execution off the main thread into N `node:worker_threads` workers. Each worker opens its own Postgres pool and runs document models in isolation. Jobs route to a worker **stickily by document id**, so all work for one document lands on the same worker \u2014 which is how per-document serialization survives the move to multiple threads.\n\nCalling `withWorkerPool` is what enables it; there is no `enabled` flag.\n\n```typescript\nconst reactor = await new ReactorBuilder()\n  .withDocumentModelSources([\n    { packageName: \"@my-org/account-document-model\", subpath: \"document-models\" },\n  ])\n  .withWorkerPool({ numWorkers: 4, db: { host: \"localhost\", port: 5432, /* ... */ } })\n  .build();\n```\n\nTwo hard requirements, and the notable thing is that both are enforced up front rather than at runtime.\n\n**Importable sources.** Workers re-import document models across the thread boundary, so a live module object cannot cross. Models must be registered as `{ filePath }` or `{ packageName }` sources. `buildModule()` throws on violation: `\"withWorkerPool requires at least one worker-importable document-model source ({ filePath } or { packageName }).\"`, and for a model registered only as a live module, `\"withWorkerPool requires worker-importable sources, but these models were registered only as live modules: ...\"`. A live module for the same `documentType@version` may coexist as long as an importable source covers it. Sources resolve in one pass \u2014 file and package sources are imported host-side and their exports scanned for `DocumentModelModule` values \u2014 so host and workers are derived from the same list and cannot diverge.\n\n**Real Postgres.** PGlite cannot be shared across threads, so parent and workers must point at the same Postgres instance. When the pool carries a `db`, the builder builds the parent's database from that same config unless `withKysely` overrides it.\n\nConnection info, by contrast, is a *compile-time* guarantee: `WorkerPoolOptions` is a union requiring either `db` or a custom `factory`, making an enabled pool without connection info unrepresentable. `DbConfig` crosses worker IPC so it must be JSON-clonable; `ssl: true` maps to `{ rejectUnauthorized: false }`, `poolSize` to pg's `max`. The optional `verifier` is off by default \u2014 omit it and workers perform no executor-side signature verification, matching the in-process executor.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/07-StorageAndScaling.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:36:11.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:11.000Z"
    }
  },
